  "rationale": "Repair of trial-af78dd3283, which wrapped the observed prefill call 900c23e99c808d2c9bda215a (Qwen3ForCausalLM, kwargs input_ids=[1,256] int64 / use_cache=True / logits_to_keep=1) in CUDA-graph capture-and-replay and was rejected after the quality run failed on both continuous steps with identical, deterministic statistics (output.logits: 41.5% of elements mismatched, max abs 5.0625 at (0,21,137522), max rel 27648 at (0,23,82333)); coverage showed both invocations took the graph route with no fallback and candidate_diagnostics recorded no exceptions, so the replay itself ran to completion. Reading 41.5% as ~13 of 32 fully-diverged decode positions, the candidate's greedy rollout matched the reference for early steps and flipped at a late near-tie: the captured kernels were selected in a different memory-pool/workspace context than the eager parent, so prefill logits/KV differed at rounding level and an argmax flipped, breaking require_exact_greedy_tokens (the logits tolerance itself would have passed). The earlier Triton attempt (trial-9a65eeeca9, recorded in the prior candidate's manifest docstring) failed the same way (max abs 2.25, 32.4% mismatch), so this workload punishes any numerical perturbation of prefill. This attempt therefore keeps the parent's exact eager aten operator chain and removes only host-side Python dispatch. Measured motivation: the warm prefill spans ~47.5 ms wall with only ~12.1 ms GPU-active across 2145 kernels (median inter-kernel gap ~9.8 us, execution_timeline-1221e205.json), i.e. ~35 ms of host-induced gaps, and python_runtime-aea48e29.json shows one invocation burning host time in 17,472 nn.Module _call_impl frames plus GradientCheckpointingLayer/capture_outputs/merge_with_config_defaults wrappers, attention-interface lookups and config __getattribute__ layers. The composite drives the identical op sequence (F.linear via torch._C._nn.linear, the exact RMSNorm op chain, HF rotate_half, matmul-based RoPE with the parent's .float() cast of the bf16-migrated inv_freq buffer, sdpa with is_causal=True/enable_gqa=True/scale=head_dim**-0.5, silu-MLP) from one lean Python loop using the module's own parameter tensors, operand order, shapes, strides and dtypes, entirely in the eager allocator (no CUDA Graph pools, no kernel re-selection). The only deviations are exact-identity eliminations: RoPE '* attention_scaling' with scaling 1.0, 'arange + 0' position ids for the empty cache, the cat against an empty KV tensor (keys are already the exact contiguous tensor the cat would produce; values are materialized .contiguous() exactly like the parent's cat output), and final-norm/lm_head rows other than the last position (row-wise reductions). The returned past_key_values is a real transformers DynamicCache whose per-layer DynamicLayer state (is_initialized/dtype/device/keys/values) matches what DynamicCache(config=...) plus update produces, so the untouched parent decode loop extends it identically. Bit-exactness was verified on CPU with the worker's Python against the installed transformers 5.16.1 parent using the real geometry (GQA 32:8, head_dim 128, bf16, [1,256] prompt, tied lm_head): torch.equal on prefill logits, every per-layer K/V tensor, and multiple decode steps driven through the composite-produced cache, plus deterministic-repeat and fallback comparisons. Route labels report the actual path per call (prefill_bitexact_eager_composite, prefill_parent_signature_fallback, prefill_runtime_failure_parent_fallback, and a retained concise prefill_setup_failure_parent_fallback category). Decode-phase calls, sampling semantics, batch/sequence/generation counts, data and thresholds are untouched, and nothing fixture-dependent is cached: each invocation recomputes from the live input_ids.",
  "setup_work": {
    "summary": "Installation-time work is host-only introspection of the live model: config validation (sdpa attention, full_attention layer types, no sliding window, silu activation, layer-count and geometry consistency), capture of per-layer parameter/bias/RMSNorm-eps references into plain Python tuples, the RoPE inv_freq reference and attention_scaling, and construction of one prototype DynamicCache(config=model.config) whose attribute dict (minus layers) and per-layer classes are snapshotted for building fresh, structurally identical caches per invocation.",
    "parameter_transforms": "None. All weights are referenced in place; bit-exactness requires the original layouts, so no packing, fusing, transposition or dtype conversion is performed.",
    "gpu_work": "None at build time: no CUDA allocations, kernels, streams, capture or replay. The first composite execution performs the same GPU work as the parent prefill.",
    "memory_effect": "No CUDA Graph pools or other driver allocations are created, so reserved memory is unaffected; setup retains only small Python objects. Per-invocation transients mirror the parent's minus 36 empty-tensor KV cat copies, 2 RoPE scalar muls, 1 arange add and 255/256 of the final-norm/logits-bound tensors, so peak_allocated_bytes should be essentially unchanged and slightly lower.",
    "fixture_dependence": "None: nothing about the known prompt, tokens or logits is captured; every invocation computes from the current input_ids."
  },
  "quality_risks": [
    "Exact-token fidelity is enforced by construction (identical aten chain, operand order, shapes, strides, dtypes, eager allocator) rather than by tolerance; CPU verification with torch.equal covers prefill logits, all per-layer KV tensors and multi-step decode through the produced cache. If an unforeseen GPU dispatch-level difference existed, the 0.02 logits tolerance would still pass and the residual risk would be a late near-tie argmax flip - the exact failure mode of the rejected CUDA-graph attempt, avoided here because no kernel re-selection or memory-pool change is introduced.",
    "Structural cache equivalence assumes transformers 5.16.1 DynamicCache semantics (layers of DynamicLayer with keys/values tensors and is_initialized/dtype/device attributes); build() derives everything from the installed model and falls back to the parent with a concise setup-failure label if the structure differs.",
    "Guarded scope: only kwargs-style calls matching the observed signature (input_ids [1,N>=2] int64 on the model device, use_cache=True, logits_to_keep=1, other known kwargs None) take the composite; anything else, including decode-shaped calls and unexpected kwargs, routes to the parent callable.",
    "Exact-identity eliminations (empty-tensor KV cat, RoPE *1.0 scaling, arange+0, non-last-position final-norm rows) mean a handful of observed aten call specs will not recur in their observed shapes even though the numerical results are unchanged.",
    "Decode-phase execution and decode_tokens_per_second are deliberately unchanged; only the ttft_ms boundary (prefill + argmax up to the explicit synchronize) is optimized."
  ],
